# MadGraph5 batch script: qt qt~ > o8 o8 NP<=2
# in vibegraph_toy_UFO, restricted by restrict_dcolor.dat.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   The symmetric structure constant d(1,2,3), which this crate's colour algebra
#   can represent and no validated process has ever exercised: the Standard Model
#   writes `f` and `T` and never `d`. It sits on the cubic self-coupling of a real
#   colour-octet scalar, so the s-channel diagram that carries it interferes with
#   the t- and u-channel quark exchanges that do not, and the reduction
#   d(a,b,c) = 2 Tr(a,b,c) + 2 Tr(c,b,a) is visible in the colour matrix rather
#   than only in a total.
#
# The model path is repo-relative to the vendored UFO; build.sh rewrites it to
# the work-area copy it stages under output/models/. This model is ours, so its
# restrict cards live inside the model directory and are staged with it.
#
# `display interactions` prints the count MadGraph's own interaction splitting
# arrives at (one interaction per coupling-order tuple, import_ufo.add_interaction)
# into the build log, which is where extract_interactions.py reads it from.
#
# The order bound is explicit on every row of this model: an unbounded generate
# runs MadGraph's WEIGHTED search, which would drop diagrams the interference
# needs.
import model validation/ufo/vibegraph_toy_UFO-dcolor
display interactions
generate qt qt~ > o8 o8 NP<=2
output qqx_to_o8o8_toy_dcolor -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
